3. Bb5+ { A calmer way to play: check first and keep the pawn, avoiding the sharper lines with c4 and d4. } 3... Bd7 4. Bc4 { Keeps the extra pawn for now. The bishop stays on its good diagonal and White follows with d3 or Nf3. } 4... Bg4 5. f3 Bf5 6. Nc3 c6 7. dxc6 Nxc6 8. Nge2 { Develops without blocking the f-pawn. Plan: castle, then d4 with a healthy extra pawn and a calm position. } *
